</ul><h1>Thanks To You</h1><p>Happy Thanksgiving, all! Today we’re selling some Steam &amp; Go Laundry Sheets. 180 of them, to be exact, which can be torn in half to clean 360 loads of laundry. Because we just know you’re going to spill some gravy on one of your nice shirts.</p>
<p>But really, today’s not about commerce. It’s about giving thanks. Which is why we wanted to use this space to tell you what we’re thankful for this year here at Meh.</p>
<p>To name just a few things:</p>
<p><strong>The ChemiCoffee Company</strong></p>
<p>Some burnt-tasting free coffee in the staff lounge? Pfft! How about free freshly roasted coffee all throughout the office, and even bags to take and brew at home?</p>
<p>That’s what we get here at Meh thanks to our partnership with the ChemiCoffee Company, and we are just so grateful. What’s more, the beans we get aren’t the usual stuff you find at the store (although, actually, you don’t find many of ChemiCoffee’s offerings at the grocery store; they mostly wholesale to the military). No, instead, we get to try their experimental new offerings. And it’s all provided in unlimited quantities, free of charge, save for filling out a short weekly survey consisting of the same four questions:</p>
<ul>
<li>Any tingling? (Just a little bit!)</li>
<li>How are your muscles feeling? (Huge!)</li>
<li>How would you describe your attitude after consuming a cup of ChemiCoffee? (Loyal!)</li>
<li>Within the first three hours of drinking a cup of ChemiCoffee, what do you see when you close your eyes? (The heat outlines of all people and animals around me!)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Themed Days</strong></p>
<p>Casual Fridays? What is this, the 1950s?</p>
<p>How about Maverick Mondays (everyone dresses like a <em>Top Gun</em> character)?</p>
<p>Or Terrapin Tuesdays (everyone wears a huge shell on their back)?</p>
<p>Or Wearable-Tech Wednesday (everyone gets a FREE shirt with sensors sewed into the seams, allowing the company to track our movements and give constructive feedback to improve our performance)?</p>
<p>Or Thimble Thursdays (best thimble-wearer gets to sew the tracking devices into the shirts for the next Wearable-tech Wednesday)?</p>
<p>Or Fire-Stopper Fridays (everyone dresses in flame-resistant gear and brings a fire extinguisher to work to do shifts fighting the fire that’s been raging in the tunnels beneath our office for decades)?</p>
<p>Or everyone’s favorite, Pretend-It’s-Maverick-Monday-on-Saturday (we’re required to come back into the office and pretend it’s a workday, but we get to dress as a <em>Top Gun</em> character AGAIN!)?</p>
<p>Themed days show us the c-suite values fun, and for that, we couldn’t be more thankful.</p>
<p><strong>The Thing Living In The Vents</strong></p>
<p>This one might be controversial. After all, can you give thanks to something that you’ve never actually seen but only heard? And even then, <em>should</em> you give thanks to something whose sharp cries occasionally leave us feeling emotionally fallow and spent?</p>
<p>Sure you can.</p>
<p>Especially when it stops shrieking and emits the low hum that leaves us all feeling exuberant and warm inside.</p>
<p><strong>You</strong></p>
<p>Look, these other things? They’re fun and all, but what we’re really thankful for today and all days is you, our wonderful customers. Because you make this site what it is: a strange, delightful community. And also because you give us your money in exchange for some really stupid products.</p>
<p>So, thank you! And again, Happy Thanksgiving!</p>